Write an SQL query to validate that every new user registration in a 'users' table has a unique email and a non-empty password field. Test your query by inserting both valid and invalid records, then verify the results.
Answer:

SELECT email, COUNT(*) FROM users
GROUP BY email
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;

SELECT * FROM users
WHERE password IS NULL OR password = '';

